   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp3ppp/2n2n2/3pp3/3P4/2PB3P/PP3PP1/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 0 7",
   "line": [
    "e5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Rather than a passive Exchange, Black strikes with e5 — accepting an isolated d-pawn in return for free, active piece play and the initiative. This is the fighting choice, not the quiet main line.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "You can answer the drawish Exchange with an e5 break, taking on an isolated pawn for activity.",
   "plans": "Open the centre, activate the pieces, win the bishop pair."
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 148,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp3ppp/2n2n2/3pP3/8/2PB3P/PP3PP1/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 0 7",
   "line": [
    "dxe5"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 14,
   "t": 149,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp3ppp/5n2/3pn3/8/2PB3P/PP3PP1/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 0 8",
   "line": [
    "Nxe5"
   ],
   "spoken": "After the trades the knight lands on e5, a fine central post, and Black is poised to win the bishop pair — the concrete pay-off for accepting the isolated pawn.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "An isolated queen's pawn buys active pieces and often the two bishops; that activity is the compensation."
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 160,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp3ppp/5n2/3pn3/8/2PB1N1P/PP3PP1/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 1 8",
   "line": [
    "Nf3"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
